# Edit Modbus read ranges in their own module settings dialog

Draft · lane full · spec rev 6 · gauntlet green at 40b290a

## Why
Modbus read ranges are edited in a separate module settings dialog (`:module`), so loading a module from a device-config file keeps that file's ranges.

## Scenarios
The 6 scenarios of #398: S1 Change read ranges on a running client · S2 A malformed range is refused · S3 Leaving the dialog without saving · S4 Loading a module keeps the device file's ranges · S5 Editing a module keeps its ranges · S6 No module settings on a monitor tab

